#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""weir — recursive occupancy join of a merge-of-merges.

ford joins parent *trees*. A merge-parent that is itself a merge then
contributes its snapshot (TRUE at kizu 0ea3916) into the next merge
(21ae074), so T⊓T looks like preserve and first-parent TRUE starts at
PR #2. Occupancy of the introducing weir never flowed.

weir: a merge-parent that is itself a merge contributes its occupancy
lattice, not its tree. Default meet (--all): TRUE iff every parent
occupancy is TRUE. --any: TRUE if any parent occupancy is TRUE.
Refuse to call birth at a merge whose parents already held TRUE.
--follow is berth, not this object. --boolean that would downcast
UNKNOWN/SHALLOW/EMPTY is a refuse (a labelled lie otherwise).

Statuses stay TRUE / FALSE / UNKNOWN / SHALLOW / EMPTY.
git log --reverse is --list. Do not pretend it is the lattice.
"""

